OL,3,GNEWSAOff-duty nurse saves man 'minutes
OL,4,Afrom death' in cardiac arrest
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man who was "minutes from death"
OL,7,Fafter suffering a cardiac arrest in the
OL,8,Fstreet has made a "miraculous" recovery
OL,9,Fafter an off-duty nurse stepped in to
OL,10,Fhelp save him, a hospital says.
OL,12,FMike Brereton, 61, was walking along
OL,13,FHigh Street in Tarporley when he
OL,14,Fsuffered a "massive heart attack" that
OL,15,Fsent him into a cardiac arrest.
OL,17,FAmong those who rushed to help him was
OL,18,FLauren Wall, who was returning home
OL,19,Ffrom a night shift at the Countess of
OL,20,FChester Hospital and said it was "just
OL,21,Fmiraculous" that he had survived such a
OL,22,Fmajor out-of-hospital health incident.
OL,23,APub: 10-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,407,400,260,160,0,100
